d. perbuatan yang mengakibatkan ketergantungan  ekonomi dengan cara membatasi dan/atau melarang  untuk bekerja yang layak di dalam atau di luar rumah  sehingga korban berada dibawah kendali orang  terse but.

translated_text:
Article 10
Neglect as referred to in Article 6 letter d is caused by:
a. acts that result in the failure to fulfill the needs of a child properly, whether physical, mental, spiritual or social, committed by parents, guardians, or any other party responsible for their care;
b. acts of deliberately neglecting to maintain, care for, or manage as appropriate committed by parents, guardians, or any other party responsible for their care;
c. acts that neglect a person within the scope of their household, whereas according to the law applicable to them or due to an agreement or contract they are obligated to provide livelihood, care, or maintenance to that person; and/or;
d. acts that result in economic dependence by means of restricting and/or prohibiting decent work inside or outside the home so that the victim is under the control of that person.

text:
BABV
HAK KORBAN
Pasal 13
Setiap korban berhak mendapatkan:
a. perlindungan;
b. informasi;
c. pelayanan optimal;
d. penanganan berkelanjutan sampai tahap  rehabilitasi; I
e. penanganan secara rahasia;
f. pendampingan secara psikologis dan hukum; dan  g. jaminan atas hak-hak yang berkaitan dengan  status korban sebagai anggota keluarga maupun  anggota masyarakat.

translated_text:
CHAPTER V
RIGHTS OF VICTIMS
Article 13
Every victim has the right to obtain:
a. protection;
b. information;
c. optimal services;
d. continuous handling up to the rehabilitation stage; I
e. confidential handling;
f. psychological and legal assistance; and g. guarantee of rights related to the victim's status as a family member as well as a member of society.

text:
Pasal 14
Selain hak-hak sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 13,  anak korban kekerasan juga mendapatkan hak-hak  khusus meliputi:
a. hak penghormatan atas kelangsungan hidup,  tumbuh dan berkembang;
b. hak pelayanan dasar; 1
c. hak perlindungan yang sama;
d. hak be bas dari berbagai stigma; dan/ a tau  e. hak mendapatkan kebebasan;
f. hak korban dan keluarga untuk mendapatkan  kemudahan dalam proses peradilan.

translated_text:
Article 14
In addition to the rights as referred to in Article 13, child victims of violence also receive special rights including:
a. the right to respect for survival, growth and development;
b. the right to basic services; 1
c. the right to equal protection;
d. the right to be free from various stigma; and/or e. the right to obtain freedom;
f. the right of victims and families to obtain facilitation in the judicial process.

text:
BAB VI
TUGAS DAN KEWAJIBAN PEMERINTAH DAERAH  Pasal 15 (1) Pemerintah Daer ah bertugas melakukan upaya upaya pencegahan, Pynanganan dan pemulihan  korban kekerasan terhadap Perempuan dan Anak,  dengan melakukan :
a. mengumpulkan data dan informasi ten tang  Perempuan dan Anak Korban Kekerasan;
b. melakukan sosialisasi peraturan perundang undangan yang berkaitan dengan perlindungan  Perempuan dan Anak Korban Kekerasan;
c. mengadakan pendidikan tentang nilai-nilai anti  kekerasan terhadap anak dan perempuan; dan  d. mengadakan pemantauan dan evaluasi terhadap  penyelenggaraan perlindungan Perempuan dan  Anak korban kekerasan.
(2) Pemerintah Daerah berkewajiban melakukan upaya upaya pencegahan, penanganan dan pemulihan  korban kekerasan terhadap Perempuan dan Anak,  menyediakan dan menyelenggarakan layanan bagi  korban dalam bentuk:
a. menyediakan dan memfasilitasi terbe n tuknya  pelayanan terpadu untuk korban dengan  melibatkan lembaga dan unsur masyarakat;
b. mendorong kepedulian masyarakat ten.tang  pentingnya perlindungan terhadap korban; dan  c. melakukan pemberdayaan masyarakat untuk  pencegahan tindak kekerasan.

translated_text:
CHAPTER VI
DUTIES AND OBLIGATIONS OF REGIONAL GOVERNMENT Article 15 (1) The Regional Government has the duty to undertake prevention efforts, handling and recovery of victims of violence against Women and Children, by:
a. collecting data and information about Women and Children Victims of Violence;
b. conducting socialization of laws and regulations related to the protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence;
c. providing education about anti-violence values toward children and women; and d. conducting monitoring and evaluation of the implementation of protection for Women and Children victims of violence.
(2) The Regional Government has the obligation to undertake prevention efforts, handling and recovery of victims of violence against Women and Children, providing and organizing services for victims in the form of:
a. providing and facilitating the establishment of integrated services for victims by involving institutions and community elements;
b. encouraging community awareness about the importance of protection for victims; and c. conducting community empowerment for the prevention of acts of violence.

