translated_text:
CHAPTER VII
INSTITUTION FOR THE IMPLEMENTATION OF PROTECTION FOR VICTIMS
Article 16
(1) The Regional Government establishes an Integrated Service Center (PPT) as the Institution for the Implementation, Prevention and Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence in the region.
(2) The PPT as referred to in paragraph (1) consists of elements:
a. health;
b. psychologist;
c. law enforcement;
d. social and empowerment;
e. education and religious affairs;
f. non-governmental organizations; and
g. private sector.
(3) Further provisions regarding the PPT as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.

text:
BAB VIII
PENCEGAHAN TINDAK KEKERASAN
Pasal 17
(1) Pemerintah dalam upaya untuk mencegah terjadi  tindak kekerasan terhadap perempuan dan anak  melakukan pemberdayaan terhadap keluarga, orang  tua, masyarakat dengan memberikan informasi,  bimbingan dan atau penyuluhan.
(2) Selain pemberdayaan dan penyandaran  sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1), pemerintah  daerah melakukan upaya sebagai berikut:
a. meningkatkan jumlah dan mutu pendidikan baik  formal maupun nonformal dan informal;
b. membuka aksebilitas untuk memperoleh  pendidikan, pelatihan, pendanaan, peningkatan  pendapatan dan pelayanan sosial;
c. mengupayakan terciptanya lapangan kerja bagi perempuan;
d. membangun partisipasi dan keperdulian  masyarakat terhadap pencegahan dan dari  tindakan kekerasan terhadap perempuan dan  anak;
e. membangun dan menyediakan system inforrnasi  yang lengkap dan mudah diakses;
f. membangun jejaring dan kerjasama dengan  penegak hukum, aparatur pemerintah, perguruan  dan berbagi lembaga swadaya masyerakat yang  bergerak dan atau peduli terhadap perempuan  dan anak korban kekerasan.

translated_text:
CHAPTER VIII
PREVENTION OF ACTS OF VIOLENCE
Article 17
(1) The Government in efforts to prevent the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children shall conduct empowerment of families, parents, the community by providing information, guidance and or counseling.
(2) In addition to empowerment and support as referred to in paragraph (1), the regional government shall undertake efforts as follows:
a. increase the quantity and quality of education both formal and nonformal and informal;
b. open accessibility to obtain education, training, funding, income enhancement and social services;
c. endeavor to create employment opportunities for women;
d. build community participation and concern towards prevention and from acts of violence against women and children;
e. build and provide a complete and easily accessible information system;
f. build networks and cooperation with law enforcers, government apparatus, universities and various non-governmental organizations that work and or care for women and children victims of violence.

